WEBVTT

00:00:00.030 --> 00:01:00.030
<b>Summary of previous episodes</b>

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:06.520
<i>Last time on </i>Frankenstein Family<i>...</i>

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.170
<i>The side effects of the medicine</i>

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:14.030
<i>turned Aisuri-neesan into a giant
 spider, and she ran rampant.</i>

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:20.020
<i>While suffering under the 
same painful side effects,</i>

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.620
<i>Ashisu-neesan gently stopped her.</i>

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.830
<i>Their appearances used to be identical, 
but now they look totally different.</i>

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:34.190
<i>But they still understand 
each other best of all.</i>

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:36.650
<i>Having siblings sure is great, huh?</i>

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:43.470
<i>Once they were back to normal, 
the landlord caught up with us in a panic.</i>

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:48.810
<i>Seeing how concerned he 
was despite the danger,</i>

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:53.110
<i>I started wondering if maybe 
we could really trust him.</i>

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:23.210
<b>Frankenstein Family</b>

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.970
Stop it!

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:42.490
<b>#8: Observation</b>

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.760
Give it back!

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:48.680
So annoying...

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:50.910
Throw this crap away!

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:54.260
It's important to my research!

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:57.030
You don't realize how hard 
it was to get this!

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:01.640
Don't you know how much we've 
suffered because of those things?!

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:03.160
You monster!

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:09.040
Don't worry. We won't use 
the medicine anymore.

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:17.940
<i>It's only a stopgap anyway. It's not perfect.</i>

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:19.260
<i>Most of all...</i>

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:27.750
<i>No matter what you look 
like, you're still Aisuri.</i>

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:33.810
<i>It has those terrible side effects...</i>

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:36.720
<i>This is just a hypothesis,</i>

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:42.230
<i>but I think the landlord 
might be willing to help us.</i>

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:45.390
<i>I need to figure him out.</i>

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:48.470
<i>Is he really someone we can depend on?</i>

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:00.360
Good morning!

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:01.010
Hey.

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:02.470
Good morning!

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.260
Morning!

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:08.280
I thought I'd get you some 
new furniture for your rooms.

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:10.140
Can we eat?

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:14.730
Ah, hot, hot!

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:17.110
Are you going to go out to buy it now?

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:19.480
I bought it on the 'net.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:22.190
The seller actually lives on the island.

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:24.410
Yeah, looks great!

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:24.410
Looks delicious!

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:29.460
Materials on this island are 
transported via waterways.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:32.580
So buying large items can be a real handful.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:42.670
Secondhand Store

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:42.670
Cabinets<Bedroom<Closet

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:42.670
Closet   Organized Wardrobe

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.970
And there are only so many 
shops on the island...

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:38.800
So everyone worked together 
to open up an online shop.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:41.030
It's mainly for information exchange,

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:43.800
but there's also a thread for 
buying and selling furniture.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.080
I see!

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:47.720
Tanisu, what's the "net"?

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:51.180
What? You don't know about the internet?

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:53.890
Well, our old life was basically like priso—

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:59.260
<i>Did Tanisu just let something
 particularly strange slip?</i>

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:02.610
I thought you were gonna observe!

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:04.950
Sorry, I got careless.

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:10.200
I've been thinking... you all seem a 
bit naive about how the world works...

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.730
But Tanisu-kun, you seem less so.

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:15.910
Well... I am a genius, after all.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:17.880
<i>A genius?</i>

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.630
<i>What's with the silence?!</i>

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:32.690
Once you're finished eating, 
let's all go visit the seller.

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:34.060
Yay!

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:39.020
He seems like a good person!

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:41.450
I wonder...

00:06:03.770 --> 00:06:07.690
You think it's okay to leave 
Suishi and Ashisu behind?

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:13.230
I bet they're pretty tired after yesterday,
 so we should let them rest today.

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:14.010
Wow! Can I eat that?

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:30.780
Hey, you two! Let's go already!

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:34.190
Don't worry. Take your time deciding.

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:36.830
I was thinking that on the way 
to picking up the furniture,

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:39.220
we could look around at all kinds of things.

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:40.230
What kinds of things?

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:43.540
We'll be living together for a while, I think.

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:47.410
I mentioned it this morning, but living 
on an island can be inconvenient.

00:06:47.410 --> 00:06:49.550
People come and go a lot.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:53.960
I was hoping you'd come to like this place.

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:56.060
Anyway, I think it's about time!

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:00.560
Let's head to the next place!

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:01.310
Okay!

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:07.640
This is a bulletin board for residents.

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:14.230
If you need anything, or you want to tell 
someone something, put a note here.

00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:16.200
Lots of people will see it.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:20.680
And here's a picture of the 
furniture we're buying!

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:21.820
Secondhand Items for Sale

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.830
Wow, looks great!

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:25.340
Right?

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.380
Uh-oh!

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:31.840
Stop it!

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:32.700
Stupid Tanisu!

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:34.830
You know I'm a genius!

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:38.450
Are you babysitting today?

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:40.350
There's a bit of a story behind it...

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:41.640
Mr. Landlord.

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:44.730
You keep getting too distracted!

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:47.270
S-Sorry.

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:51.140
Aren't you supposed to be 
teaching us about the island?

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:52.280
What, feeling lonely?

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:53.350
Here.

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:54.780
No! No way!

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:59.790
I just want to see the furniture 
as soon as possible!

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:02.250
Got it, got it. We'll stop by one more place.

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:03.730
Thank you! Come again!

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:03.730
Then we'll go right to the furniture.

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:04.790
Ah, thanks.

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:07.000
Tastes weird.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.590
I think it's pretty tasty, actually.

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:16.030
We're here.

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:19.130
Hey, Wei.

00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:20.220
Hey.

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:23.220
Almost everything sold here is secondhand.

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:27.160
And all the profits go to 
help the island's animals!

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:30.780
Um, who are these kids?

00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:34.170
Hey, you're the teacher who was 
with Sumire-chan yesterday.

00:08:34.170 --> 00:08:37.570
Some things happened, 
and now I'm looking after them!

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:41.830
You think you're some kind
 of philanthropist now?

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:44.780
Oh, well, er...

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:17.940
Someone had put some used 
furniture on the web,

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:21.450
so I thought we'd all come out 
together and haul it back.

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:23.300
Speaking of used...

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:27.580
Everything you're wearing 
is stuff we sold here.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:29.050
That might be true.

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:32.850
We always get our clothes 
out of the recycling box.

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:34.090
Oh, I see.

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:37.520
You put kids in secondhand clothes,
 buy them secondhand furniture,

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:40.520
and even bring them out 
here to make them help you.

00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:43.590
What a <i>spectacular</i> caregiver you are.

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:47.030
Let's go.

00:09:48.570 --> 00:09:52.050
<i>That brutal sarcasm... 
she's a lot like Suishi-neesan.</i>

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:54.320
C'mon, let's go.

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:02.080
What?!

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:03.410
It's gone?!

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:07.720
Remember, you said you wanted 
to see it before deciding!

00:10:07.720 --> 00:10:10.490
But someone else wanted it right away.

00:10:10.490 --> 00:10:13.210
Who wouldn't choose the sure thing, you know?

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:15.080
Oh, come on...

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:17.630
You could have at least contacted me...

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:20.300
I forgot, okay? Sorry.

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:21.960
Anyway, I think we're done here!

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:33.690
<i>I messed up...</i>

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:37.430
<i>I got their hopes up, and 
then basically betrayed them.</i>

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:40.210
<i>They must be so disappointed...</i>

00:10:40.210 --> 00:10:43.280
<i>There's the two girls at home, too...</i>

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:46.460
For an adult, you're not 
very useful, are you?

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:50.000
Utterly useless. I was right 
not to get my hopes up.

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:54.310
I'm sorry! We should have gone right 
to get it instead of wasting time.

00:10:54.820 --> 00:11:00.040
It's not much of an apology, but I'll 
buy you new furniture right now.

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:01.900
What's come over him?

00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:02.640
Dunno.

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:07.720
Suishi mentioned before that 
he overthinks everything.

00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:12.350
I was hoping you'd come to like this place.

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.230
Kuma-san.

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:19.110
Can I call you that?

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:21.230
Y-Yeah.

00:11:22.210 --> 00:11:24.120
It's okay.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:28.330
There's another nice place on this island.

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:36.150
By "nice place"...

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:38.590
you meant the dump?

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:40.600
Found me a treasure!

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:42.680
You can call it trash, but...

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:49.810
As far as I can see, there's tons 
of stuff here we can still use!

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:55.360
The TV in our room is something 
Tanisu found and repaired, too.

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:58.130
I told you I'd buy it, though!

00:11:58.130 --> 00:11:59.880
There's no need to risk hurting yourselves

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:02.410
searching for things you can recycle!

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:05.870
It's not about that.

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:10.330
It just feels like a waste to throw 
out things you can still use.

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:14.330
But you were looking forward to it, 
too, weren't you?

00:12:16.230 --> 00:12:18.840
It's true that it's nice to have new things.

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:23.640
But there's something nice about using 
things people don't want anymore

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:24.800
as if they were new.

00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:27.850
<i>They really are strange children...</i>

00:12:29.170 --> 00:12:31.550
<i>People like new things.</i>

00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:33.260
<i>That goes double for children.</i>

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:35.310
Found you!

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:37.310
Something for Ashisu and Suishi...

00:12:38.810 --> 00:12:42.680
<i>But they all share a desire 
not to let things go to waste.</i>

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:44.810
I am a genius, after all!

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:47.190
<i>Little Genius.</i>

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:49.370
I'll help, too!

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:52.720
<i>Yu-chan, hey.</i>

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:56.040
<i>I think you and these kids 
might just get along!</i>

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:08.400
Okay!

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:10.570
We've finished everyone's new furniture!

00:13:13.490 --> 00:13:14.550
You okay?

00:13:14.550 --> 00:13:15.480
I'm fine.

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:16.570
Getting a cold?

00:13:16.570 --> 00:13:19.560
It's your fault for not 
reserving the furniture!

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:21.900
Aisuri, that's going too far.

00:13:27.130 --> 00:13:29.520
This room's too small.

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:31.110
We don't have a choice!

00:13:31.110 --> 00:13:35.290
No one else would take us 
in on such short notice.

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:37.510
Stupid Tanisu!

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:43.300
I don't think the girls want to 
sleep in the same bed as us...

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:46.100
Oh, is that it?

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:50.350
Tanisu and I will sleep on the floor. 
You three can take the bed.

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:54.830
I don't mind, but you'll catch 
a cold if you sleep on the floor.

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:57.050
There's no proper furniture.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.400
Fine!

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:05.860
I'll figure out something, 
so you guys rest easy.

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:12.240
And now...

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:13.330
Almost got it.

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:19.740
What's wrong?

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:25.770
Aisuri thinks you must be 
tired. She wants to help.

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:27.380
Shut up!

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:30.310
Thank you, Aisuri!

00:14:30.310 --> 00:14:32.170
N-No problem!

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:39.710
<i>It was all trash, but we 
worked hard together...</i>

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:46.590
<i>We made a comfortable place for ourselves.</i>

00:14:46.590 --> 00:14:48.320
<i>It's our new home!</i>

00:14:54.730 --> 00:14:57.870
You can put a lot of stuff 
in big shelves like these!

00:14:58.520 --> 00:15:00.190
They can fit anything!

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:04.750
I think we have the result 
of our observation.

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:05.750
Yeah.

00:15:07.450 --> 00:15:09.470
I can't wait for tomorrow!

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:49.980
<b>Frankenstein Extras!</b>

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:46.670
<i>Frankenstein Extras!</i>

00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:49.980
<b>Report No. 2</b>

00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:49.980
<i>Anime Japan Report.</i>

00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:52.920
<b>Held in March 2018, it's Japan's biggest
 anime event, Anime Japan 2018!</b>

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:55.700
<b>The attendance over four days was 152,331!</b>

00:16:56.050 --> 00:17:01.240
<b>March 25th: Akatsuki Rin-san appears at the 
Frankenstein Family booth to perform the OP!</b>

00:17:01.510 --> 00:17:05.600
<b>We asked some questions to the attendees, too!</b>

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:09.230
<b>If you were going to be modified,
 what power would you want?</b>

00:17:09.230 --> 00:17:12.710
Excuse me. We'd like to ask you a question.

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:15.770
The power to make anything 
I cook taste delicious.

00:17:15.770 --> 00:17:20.390
Anything I make is delicious. Even 
if I burn it, it turns out delicious.

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:23.160
The ability to make anything 
I think about real.

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:24.550
Because I'm a king.

00:17:24.550 --> 00:17:26.440
I do not wish to work.

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:29.190
The ability to remove parts of my body.

00:17:29.750 --> 00:17:31.880
Then to substitute other parts.

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:33.160
That's what I want.

00:17:33.160 --> 00:17:35.930
Being able to change my face and such.

00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:37.780
The ability to walk on water.

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:39.930
Because I'm not a great swimmer.

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:44.360
The ability to either read minds, 
or to tell if someone's lying.

00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:48.300
The ability to move distant 
objects. I'd love that.

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:49.750
Telekinesis!

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:52.320
Because it's annoying to 
get up and fetch something!

00:17:52.320 --> 00:17:56.530
I could just wave my hand, 
and my tea would come to me.

00:17:56.530 --> 00:17:58.300
Wouldn't that be nice?

00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:02.190
The ability to warp and 
get to work right away.

00:18:02.190 --> 00:18:04.220
That would be convenient.

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:10.190
I'm not a morning person, so it would be 
a convenient way to get to work every day.

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:11.880
The ability to talk to animals.

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:13.580
I have a cat, you see.

00:18:13.580 --> 00:18:16.010
I never know what he's thinking.

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:18.700
He walks up to me, so I 
think he wants attention,

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:21.230
and then he suddenly bites me.

00:18:21.230 --> 00:18:23.320
I'm like... what?

00:18:23.320 --> 00:18:27.790
So the ability to understand 
my pet cat would be nice.

00:18:28.060 --> 00:18:30.790
<b>Talk Show Part 2</b>

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:33.420
So, things like spiders and trees...

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:37.850
Have you ever wondered why they 
chose those modifications?

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:38.880
Oh, yes!

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:39.970
There's so many options.

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:42.530
<b>Ashisu
Hayami Saori</b>

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:42.300
Why a tree? Why a spider?

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:45.740
Maybe they really didn't have many options?

00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:48.280
You guys would probably 
want cat ears and stuff.

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:49.480
<b>Yu Kaito
Horie Kazuma</b>

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:49.480
<b>Sumire
Kubo Yurika</b>

00:18:48.280 --> 00:18:49.480
Cute.

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:51.690
Men always want that.

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:52.920
<b>Tanisu
Sugiyama Riho</b>

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:52.920
<b>Suishi
Ikuta Yoshiko</b>

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:52.920
True.

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:55.670
Maybe the other options were too crazy.

00:18:55.670 --> 00:18:56.480
Like dirt.

00:18:57.590 --> 00:19:00.550
Yeah, I don't want to be dirt.

00:19:00.550 --> 00:19:02.310
Or air.

00:19:02.310 --> 00:19:04.660
Maybe all the choices were absurd.

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:09.300
When you're a child, you tend 
to choose some odd things.

00:19:09.300 --> 00:19:12.380
You write down what you 
want to be as a child,

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:14.670
and when you look back at it 
you find it very confusing.

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:15.560
Totally!

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:16.340
I see.

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:17.210
Yeah, true.

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:21.400
So your character might be modified to 
something they wanted to be as a child.

00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:23.600
Yes, I see.

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:26.910
When I was a child, I might 
have wanted to be a dinosaur.

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:28.140
I see!

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:31.540
Papa, how come no one else has to study?

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:35.610
Their bodies have been modified 
to give them special abilities.

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:38.960
But to the same degree, I can't expect 
much from them in the way of brains.

00:19:38.960 --> 00:19:40.470
At least not compared to you.

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:41.950
Great one!

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:44.990
This way!

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:47.520
Namikawa-san is great at his current role.

00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:47.880
He is.

00:19:47.880 --> 00:19:53.460
He's a modified human and dog, a half-breed.

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:58.000
<i>Aisuri-neesan seems pretty calm,</i>

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:01.240
<i>but I think the dog in Snow-niisan 
has reached its limit.</i>

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:04.580
<i>When I'm in a wide-open space, 
my dog blood starts itching!</i>

00:20:04.580 --> 00:20:08.270
First, he's great at playing a dog.

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:09.230
Dog casting?

00:20:09.230 --> 00:20:12.700
The dog is the real role.

00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:13.440
It's amazing.

00:20:16.890 --> 00:20:18.150
Let's go.

00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:23.150
Please.

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:32.480
Maybe he was cast for the role because 
his performance as a dog was so good!

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:34.480
He's really cute.

00:20:34.480 --> 00:20:37.830
Such a cute dog.

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:40.430
Sumire is the story's ordinary girl.

00:20:40.430 --> 00:20:44.090
She's just the most ordinary 
girl there is, basilly.

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:45.300
Oops, I said "basilly."

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:57.310
Oh, is that man with the 
white hair your brother?

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:00.320
Yeah, that's Snow-niisan.

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:02.670
<i>He seemed nice!</i>

00:21:02.670 --> 00:21:04.530
<i>What is it, Sumire?</i>

00:21:04.530 --> 00:21:10.450
Of the characters I've played, she's the 
most straightforward ingénue type, I think.

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:13.080
Yes, I think so.

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:16.370
She's so cute, like an angel!

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:19.620
She's cute, but I think 
she's a bit of a devil.

00:21:19.620 --> 00:21:21.120
No way!

00:21:21.120 --> 00:21:23.800
Did that come out naturally?

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:25.900
Yeah, it did.

00:21:25.900 --> 00:21:28.240
Does her thing with the 
brothers come out naturally?

00:21:28.240 --> 00:21:29.590
I think it could cause friction.

00:21:29.590 --> 00:21:33.780
She's an angel, so she loves everyone.

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:36.390
That's the devilish part!

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:39.160
That's a bit scary!

00:21:39.160 --> 00:21:43.320
Watch the next episode and decide 
if she's an angel or a devil.

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:45.420
I think men will say she's a devil.

00:21:45.420 --> 00:21:49.050
Well, she's still very young.

00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:51.950
I think she's probably not 
thinking about it that hard.

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:54.580
She's a very sweet girl.

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:56.970
Landlord! Rent income!

00:21:56.970 --> 00:21:58.190
Great to be him, huh?

00:21:58.190 --> 00:21:59.000
That's your point?

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:00.490
Why are you talking about that?

00:22:00.490 --> 00:22:05.570
I think what I'm saying is common sense, 
but he's not that kind of landlord.

00:22:05.570 --> 00:22:07.590
He's doing this out of the 
goodness of his heart.

00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:08.590
Yes, really.

00:22:08.590 --> 00:22:12.010
I mean, I'm worried that maybe 
he's not getting his rent money.

00:22:12.010 --> 00:22:15.220
He gets furniture at a secondhand shop.

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:18.780
He's more like their guardian.

00:22:18.780 --> 00:22:20.230
Yeah!

00:22:20.760 --> 00:22:22.350
Tasty!

00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:25.490
I've lost all interest in dog food.

00:22:26.070 --> 00:22:28.870
What kind of life have you kids been living?

00:22:29.800 --> 00:22:31.830
I suppose you had a nice rest?

00:22:32.490 --> 00:22:35.510
Yeah, I haven't had a bed in so long.

00:22:36.090 --> 00:22:39.500
Usually, Snow-niisan and I are
 stuck sleeping on the floor.

00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:42.500
<i>Is that why he was so grumpy last night?</i>

00:22:43.840 --> 00:22:47.550
I've played a lot of characters in my life

00:22:47.550 --> 00:22:53.550
but when I think about kind people 
like that landlord existing...

00:22:53.870 --> 00:22:59.220
It's like, it doesn't even matter 
that they're not related by blood.

00:22:59.220 --> 00:23:04.040
I think his feelings surpass blood relation.

00:23:04.040 --> 00:23:06.190
He's a great character.

00:23:06.550 --> 00:23:09.950
I hope you'll all cheer on the landlord.

00:23:09.950 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:10.820 --> 00:23:13.040
<i>Snow-niisan is sick?</i>

00:23:13.040 --> 00:23:16.120
<i>The landlord goes to the 
mainland looking for medicine,</i>

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:19.750
<i>but I'm worried about his condition, 
and I can't wait for him.</i>

00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:22.250
<i>We should look for medicine 
on the island, too!</i>

00:23:22.610 --> 00:23:24.960
<i>Suishi-neesan is staying home...</i>

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:29.490
<i>What's she doing? 
Getting info from the internet?</i>

00:23:29.490 --> 00:23:33.830
<i>That shady chatroom... it's dangerous, Sis!</i>

00:23:34.360 --> 00:23:37.470
<i>Next time on </i>Frankenstein 
Family<i>: "Nature."</i>

00:23:34.570 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>#9:  Nature</b>

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:38.700
<i>Catch it, okay?</i>
